/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Nominal cover is the design depth of concrete over all steel, including the stirrups, written on the drawing.
   - Because the nominal cover is measured to the stirrup, the main bar sits deeper: its cover is the nominal cover plus the stirrup diameter.
   - s is the clear spacing between n bars of diameter φ in one layer (mm); b is the beam width (mm); c is the nominal cover (mm); φs is the stirrup diameter (mm).
   - A stirrup is anchored when its end is bent at least 90° round a bar of at least its own diameter and continued 8φ, or bent 135° and continued 6φ, or bent 180° and continued 4φ.
   - The schedule and the drawing must agree bar for bar; the fabricator works only from the schedule.
*/
