/* book Worked example 2: Q: Write the weight lines of the bar bending schedule for the same beam over a 6.0 m clear span on 300 mm supports: four 20 mm bottom bars and two 12 mm top bars each 6.54 m long, and 10 mm stirrups at 140 mm with a cutting length of 1.72 m.
   1. Unit weights: 20 mm: 20²/162 = 2.469 kg/m; 12 mm: 144/162 = 0.889 kg/m; 10 mm: 100/162 = 0.617 kg/m.
   2. Bottom bars: 4 × 6.54 × 2.469 = 64.6 kg.
   3. Top bars: 2 × 6.54 × 0.889 = 11.6 kg.
   4. Number of stirrups: first and last 50 mm from the faces, so (6000 − 100)/140 + 1 = 43.1, round up to 44.
   5. Stirrup cutting length: centreline 230 mm × 530 mm gives 2 × (230 + 530) = 1520 mm, plus 100 mm for each 135° hook (a common site allowance) = 1720 mm. Weight: 44 × 1.72 × 0.617 = 46.7 kg.
   6. Total for these marks: 64.6 + 11.6 + 46.7 = 122.9 kg.
   Answer: Bottom bars 64.6 kg, top bars 11.6 kg, 44 stirrups 46.7 kg; 122.9 kg in all (side-face bars are listed the same way). */
